Z||000000||Carolina 88GT||02-16-2000||11:07 AM||||Came across this one over the weekend.  Cruising around town, I came across an 87GT tires going flat/cracked from having sat so long.  Factory sunroof, weatherstripping is starting to look worn (everywhere).  The front hood doesnt close and the front fascia in the middle seems to have pulled away from the center bolt.  Interior (seats) are trashed.  Engine if froze up (per original owver) missing the rear engine vent on the right side.  The right side sail panel is cracked, and the paint looks like it has been sitting in the sun for 10-12 months (which it has). She aid she would give it all up for 400.00.  What are your throughts? let it die or.....||||reg||9
Z||000001||GT Bastard||02-16-2000||12:13 PM||||If there wasn't any major rusting to speak of, I think I would go for it.  Just offer $200 bucks and see what she says.  More than likely, she'll be more than willing to part with it.  You could make it into a nice car for a reasonable price if you can do the work yourself.  If you're going to pay someone else to repair/rebuild the engine, you're probably better off without it.  Out of curiosity, where is it at?||||reg||1
